<%# Status pill.

    design.md, Status pill:

      inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 text-xs font-medium

    with a light tint and a dark foreground per tone, and **no ring and no border**. This
    component had `ring-1 ring-inset` with a per-tone ring colour, which the spec does not
    specify - and because fourteen hand-rolled badges were swept onto it, that unspecified
    stroke ended up on every badge in the app. Aligning a component is only alignment if the
    component itself matches the spec; treating whatever exists as the baseline just
    standardises the drift.

    Tones follow design.md's names, so emerald and rose rather than green and red. Measured on
    their own tints: emerald 5.21:1, rose 5.72:1, slate 6.92:1, amber 4.84:1, blue 6.16:1,
    teal 5.25:1 - all clear AA. Neutral is slate-600, not slate-500, because design.md records
    that slate-500 is 4.34:1 on the slate-100 tint.

    :info and :brand are not named in design.md; they follow the same tint/foreground shape.

    Meaning is never colour-alone: the label always states the status.

    Locals:
      label - text
      tone  - :neutral (default) :success :warning :danger :info :brand
      class - optional extra classes %>
<% tone = local_assigns.fetch(:tone, :neutral).to_sym %>
<% tones = {} %>
<% tones[:neutral] = "bg-slate-100 text-slate-600" %>
<% tones[:success] = "bg-emerald-50 text-emerald-700" %>
<% tones[:warning] = "bg-amber-50 text-amber-700" %>
<% tones[:danger] = "bg-rose-50 text-rose-700" %>
<% tones[:info] = "bg-blue-50 text-blue-700" %>
<% tones[:brand] = "bg-teal-50 text-teal-700" %>

<span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full px-2.5 py-1 text-xs font-medium <%= tones.fetch(tone, tones[:neutral]) %> <%= local_assigns[:class] %>">
  <%= label %>
</span>
